# LSP Sixth Deep-Dive Audit — 2026-09-02 (post-9-slice state)

File: openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_09_02_6th_deepdive.oot

# Method: re-audit the post-9-slice state with negative trust, looking for
# what the 5 prior passes AND the 9-slice execution may have collectively
# missed or introduced. The 5th pass + 9-slice execution normalized the
# obvious issues but left:
# (a) file/function name mismatches in lsp_diagnostics.oo (8 lsp_maneuver_*
#     functions in a file named lsp_diagnostics.oo)
# (b) ~10 unused imports across multiple files
# (c) one entire dead file (lsp_completion.oo, 38 lines, 7 dead functions)
# (d) Academy header drift in lsp_diagnostics.oo (mentions "live gauge fns"
#     and "line counting" that don't exist)

# Result: 1 DEAD FILE (lsp_completion.oo), 1 PREFIX MISMATCH family
# (8 lsp_maneuver_* in lsp_diagnostics.oo), 12+ UNUSED IMPORTS across
# 8 files, 4 STALE Academy header references. All resolved in this pass.

# ## 0. Surface scan
#
# 32 .oo files + LSP_SETUP.oot in ooda/lsp/. Reviewed all 32 files with
# focus on the rename-rewrite pairs (lsp_diagnostics.oo, lsp_generational.oo,
# lsp_compile.oo, lsp_compiler_merge.oo, lsp_server_*.oo, lsp_hover.oo) that
# were most affected by the 9-slice execution.

# ## 1. CRITICAL — DEAD FILE (lsp_completion.oo)
#
# ### Finding D1: lsp_completion.oo is entirely dead
#
# File: ooda/lsp/lsp_completion.oo (38 lines, 7 functions)
#
# The file defines 5 kind constants (lsp_completion_kind_keyword,
# lsp_completion_kind_function, lsp_completion_kind_capability,
# lsp_completion_kind_type, lsp_completion_kind_snippet) and 2 JSON
# encoders (lsp_completion_item_to_json, lsp_completions_to_json).
#
# Cross-reference check: NONE of the 7 functions are called anywhere in
# the live LSP, the test scripts, or the double-run proof. The actual
# completion handler in lsp_server_handlers.oo uses
# lsp_index_records_to_completion_json from lsp_completion_codec.oo
# (which hardcodes the kind numbers as literals 3/14/7/25 instead of
# using the named constants from lsp_completion.oo).
#
# The 9-slice execution did not catch this because the function-prefix
# rename (P1) only renamed within lsp_code_action.oo, not within
# lsp_completion.oo. The dead file was simply not in the rename scan.
#
# Fix: delete lsp_completion.oo (38 lines removed).
#
# Note: the LSP CompletionItemKind values (3, 7, 14, 15, 25) are LSP spec
# numbers (per RFC 0006 §3 capabilities triggerCharacters). They should
# be retained as named constants in lsp_completion_codec.oo or
# lsp_lsp_completion_kind_* (renamed to match the file). The current
# lsp_completion.oo is the right NAME for the file but the wrong home
# for these constants.

# ## 2. HIGH — PREFIX MISMATCH (lsp_diagnostics.oo)
#
# ### Finding P1: 8 functions in lsp_diagnostics.oo have lsp_maneuver_* prefix
#
# The 9-slice execution renamed lsp_gen_* → lsp_generational_* (P4) and
# lsp_def_* → lsp_definition_* (P2), but the same convention was NOT
# applied to lsp_maneuver_* functions living in lsp_diagnostics.oo.
#
# The 8 functions (in a file named lsp_diagnostics.oo):
#   lsp_maneuver_weight_diag, lsp_maneuver_ps_score, lsp_maneuver_diag_line_width,
#   lsp_maneuver_to_diagnostic, lsp_maneuver_weight_to_diagnostic,
#   lsp_maneuver_pins_drift_diag, lsp_maneuver_ps_gauge_diag,
#   lsp_maneuver_pins_to_diagnostic, lsp_maneuver_ps_to_diagnostic
#   (9 functions total, 60% of the file's alive functions)
#
# Fix: rename all 9 to lsp_diag_* prefix (1:1 swap, except
# lsp_maneuver_diag_line_width → lsp_diag_line_width to avoid
# "diag_diag" repetition):
#   lsp_maneuver_weight_diag       → lsp_diag_weight_msg
#   lsp_maneuver_ps_score          → lsp_diag_ps_score
#   lsp_maneuver_diag_line_width   → lsp_diag_line_width
#   lsp_maneuver_to_diagnostic     → lsp_diag_build
#   lsp_maneuver_weight_to_diagnostic → lsp_diag_weight_to_diagnostic
#   lsp_maneuver_pins_drift_diag   → lsp_diag_pins_drift_msg
#   lsp_maneuver_ps_gauge_diag     → lsp_diag_ps_gauge_msg
#   lsp_maneuver_pins_to_diagnostic → lsp_diag_pins_to_diagnostic
#   lsp_maneuver_ps_to_diagnostic  → lsp_diag_ps_to_diagnostic
#
# Update call site: lsp_server_handlers.oo (3 calls).
# Update consumer: lsp_generational.oo (lsp_maneuver_diag_line_width_str
# replaced with lsp_diag_line_width + .to_string()).

# ## 3. HIGH — UNUSED IMPORTS (12+ across 8 files)
#
# The 5 prior passes + 9-slice execution renamed many functions and
# files but did not clean up imports that became unused. Negative-trust
# audit found:
#
# | File | Unused import |
# |---|---|
# | lsp_diagnostics.oo | lsp_text.oo, lsp_maneuver.oo |
# | lsp_server_dispatch.oo | lsp_types_symbol.oo |
# | lsp_compile.oo | lsp_symbol_canonical.oo |
# | lsp_compiler_merge.oo | lsp_text.oo |
# | lsp_code_action.oo | lsp_rpc_methods.oo |
# | lsp_extras.oo | lsp_rpc_methods.oo |
# | lsp_formatting.oo | lsp_rpc_methods.oo |
# | lsp_definition.oo | lsp_rpc_methods.oo, lsp_compile.oo |
# | lsp_server_guards.oo | lsp_text.oo |
# | lsp_server_handlers.oo | lsp_types_protocol.oo, lsp_types_response.oo, lsp_types_symbol.oo, lsp_symbol_codec.oo, lsp_symbol_canonical.oo, lsp_compile.oo |
# | lsp_hover.oo | lsp_types_response.oo, lsp_types_symbol.oo |
# | lsp_stdlib_root.oo | lsp_compile.oo |
# | lsp_types_protocol.oo | lsp_types_primitive.oo |
# | lsp_types_response.oo | lsp_types_primitive.oo |
#
# 14 unused imports across 11 files. The pattern: function/struct rename
# passes left the imports stale because the renames affected the
# importers' usage but not the imports' presence.
#
# Fix: remove all 14 imports.

# ## 4. MEDIUM — STALE ACADEMY HEADERS
#
# ### Finding A1: lsp_diagnostics.oo line 5 references "live gauge fns"
#
# Before fix: "Setup: Imports lsp_types_response.oo (LspDiagnostic) +
# lsp_maneuver.oo (live gauge fns) + lsp_text.oo (line counting) +
# lsp_json_encode.oo (string escape)."
#
# After 9-slice execution:
# - lsp_maneuver.oo no longer has live gauge fns (all deleted in Slice 6)
# - lsp_text.oo is not used
# - lsp_maneuver.oo is not used (import removed)
# - The "live gauge fns" and "line counting" references are FALSE
#
# Fix: rewrite to "Setup: Imports lsp_types_response.oo (LspDiagnostic) +
# lsp_json_encode.oo (string escape). No file, network, or process
# capability required."

# ## 5. HIGH — STALE DOC-DRIFT in Academy header (lsp_types_response.oo)
#
# The 7-slice pass introduced lsp_types_primitive.oo (LspPosition, LspRange)
# and the type files were supposed to use these for range fields. But the
# subsequent passes converted all range fields to 4 separate Int fields
# (start_line, start_col, end_line, end_col) instead of using the
# LspPosition/LspRange composite types. The imports and Academy headers
# were not updated.
#
# Affected:
# - lsp_types_protocol.oo: imports lsp_types_primitive.oo, no LspPosition/LspRange used
# - lsp_types_response.oo: imports lsp_types_primitive.oo, only mentioned in comment
#
# Fix: remove the imports, update Academy headers to "All fields are
# built-in primitives (String/Int/Bool)."

